  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "26",
  "quote": "if the tenant consents to the entry at the time of entry",
  "reason": "Under the Act, a landlord may only enter without notice based on consent if the tenant consents at the time of entry, making a clause providing advance consent in the tenancy agreement inconsistent with the Act and void."
}

